<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vicus Helena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 448</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Vicus Helena was fought in the 440s, probably around 448, at an unidentified place in Artois in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. The Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> and the future emperor Majorian surprised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salian-franks">Salian Franks</a> of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodio">Chlodio</a> during a wedding celebration and defeated them. The setback did not stop Frankish expansion, and Chlodio kept the lands he had taken up to the Somme.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vicus-helena.jpg" alt="Battle of Vicus Helena" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Cplakidas · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:400_Germania_I_II_Belgica_I_II.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
